                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @decision
                                text "The parser already implements POSIX's Rule 4 boundary exactly: the first case-item token is read with CHKKWD before the optional `(` is consumed, while every pattern word after `(` or `|` is read with flags 0. Map the rule at that lexer-mode transition and strengthen the grammar corpus with reserved-word patterns proving both sides: `in` after `(` and `esac` after `|` remain WORDs, while unparenthesized `esac` in the first production is recognized as the reserved terminator and makes the following `)` invalid. Verification: all four grammar.case-clause cases, four focused parser tests, 14 harness unit tests, and git diff --check pass."
