                            {
                                at 2026-08-18T10:13:56.548887414Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @decision
                                text "Gate EOF rearming on the command loop's existing interactive-input classifier. A top-level command file or stdin script terminates at physical EOF even if it set ignoreeof; an interactive root loop with ignoreeof continues indefinitely, while the stopped-job retry cap remains unchanged. Verification: both focused POSIX cases, 14 harness tests, the complete 731-case POSIX harness, and 255 nsh core tests pass."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-18T10:13:56.638277641Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-18T11:42:49.719683972Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @errata
                                text "Model correction: the interactive-input classification must be captured when cmdloop starts. The live `inter` value is derived again after each command, so a non-interactive command file that executes `set -i` can change it; it is therefore not the input-source classifier the original decision described. A command file or stdin script remains non-interactive at physical EOF even after runtime `set -i`, while an interactive top-level loop retains ignoreeof retry behavior. The strengthened POSIX case sets both -i and ignoreeof; the 731-case harness and 255 core tests pass."
                                after_done true
                            }
                        )
                    }
                )
            }
        )
