                            {
                                at 2026-08-15T14:46:45.659532052Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "**Seventh stretch gated green on `e16491cd` and landed. The `input` and `options` rows of §5 are both complete.**\n\n```\nrunall      PASS=61592 FAIL=0 FLAKY=40 XFAIL=4, no STALE, zero .out\ndivtest     PASS=44 FAIL=0\nptydiff     PASS=43 FAIL=0 FLAKY=0   (all ten ^C, both editing modes)\nPOSIX       cases PASS=660 FAIL=51 -- the 51-name core EXACTLY,\n            zero missing, zero extra\ncargo test  200 + 26\nwarnings    74\n```\n\n**The sweep ran under contention and is still valid, for a reason worth stating rather than assumed.** An unrelated rustc bootstrap build held the box at load 30–60 for the whole run. The earlier resumption note said to re-run quiet before landing; on reading the result that is not necessary, and the argument is one-way: **load can manufacture false failures — timeouts, races, spurious divergence — but it cannot manufacture a false pass, and it cannot make a case disappear silently.** A case that timed out would be classified, not skipped. The sweep returned `PASS=61592` exactly, which is the figure every green sweep on this node has returned, with `FAIL=0`, `XFAIL=4`, no STALE and no `.out` artifacts. A regression cannot hide inside an unchanged pass total. What contention actually cost was wall clock and `FLAKY`, which is precisely what the third stretch's classifier note says it costs.\n\nCorroborating: the rustc build finished before `ptydiff` and POSIX ran, and `ptydiff` returned **FLAKY=0** — better than the FLAKY=1 an *idle* box produced two stretches ago. The two `fc` cases stayed passing, since POSIX was run from `target/debug/nsh` as `4bc87ec` now requires.\n\n**`ptydiff` is the gate that mattered most here and it was worth waiting for.** This stretch changed `preadfd`'s line-editor read path — the `mem::take` that fixes the §5.5 violation — and `runall` cannot reach it: the corpus is non-interactive, so the editor never runs. Cases 18–25 (`emacs mode: basic`, `emacs mode: fc -l`, `vi mode: basic`, `vi mode: fc -l`, `editing off then on`, `HISTSIZE in editing`, `multiline into history`) are the only coverage that edit has, and all of them pass. **The rule: when a change touches a path the corpus structurally cannot execute, the corpus being green is not evidence about it.**\n\n**Trend, per commit.**\n\n```\n3470  20800c0  previous tip\n3475  74628e7  alias bit to the input layer   +5\n3442  5af5043  input scalars                 -33\n3428  0f1da0e  input frame stack             -14\n3340  ba411ce  parser's nine                 -88\n3308  4378d0f  shellparam + minusc + optnames -32\n```\n\n**Node total 3833 → 3308, −525. `static mut` declarations 77 → 59.** `input.rs` is the first file on this node to reach zero."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-15T14:55:49.719267857Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "**Completion re-derived from the code at `0bced96`. Every remaining `static mut` is blocked, excluded by §5.1/§5.2/§5.3, not shell state, or another node's. There is no unblocked shell state left to move.**\n\n49 declarations remain, from 86 when this stretch pair began. Each read and classified.\n\n**A. Owed to `Shell`, BLOCKED — 10.** `output.rs SHELL_IO` and `streams.rs STREAMS` (one group, `public-api`'s builder — see the `io` blocker); `trap.rs`'s `trap`/`ptrap`/`trapcnt`/`sigmode` and `jobs.rs vforked` (the `onsig` presence-bit question); `eval.rs commandname`, `error.rs errlinno` and `options.rs arg0` (the diagnostic spine — all three read by `sh_warnx` for one prefix, and none should move alone).\n\n**B. Excluded by §5.1/§5.3, the signal group — 5.** `trap.rs`'s `gotsig`/`pending_sig`/`gotsigchld`, `error.rs`'s `intpending` and `suppressint`. `host-owns-signals` / the `SignalSink`.\n\n**C. §5.2 says these must not be fields — 6.** The four §5.2 names (`exec.rs pathopt`, `expand.rs argbackq`, `arith_yacc.rs arith_buf`, `bltin/test.rs t_wp`) plus `parser.rs`'s `checkkwd` and `quoteflag`, which this node found and which want the *parameter* conversion §5.2 prescribes rather than a field.\n\n**D. Per-call working state, not shell state — 17.** `arith_yacc.rs`'s `yylval`/`last_token`/`arith_startbuf`, `bltin/fc.rs`'s four `getopt` scalars and its `active` re-entrancy guard, `expand.rs`'s `exparg`/`expbuf`/`globbuf`/`ifsregions`, `exec.rs pathbuf`, `jobs.rs cmdbuf`, `bltin/cd.rs pwdbuf`, `bltin/test.rs t_wp_op`, `mystring.rs quoted`.\n\n**E. Const tables wanting the `optnames` treatment — 4.** `builtins/mod.rs bltin`, `bltin/test.rs ops`, `arith_yylex.rs arith_names`, `mystring.rs nullstr`. Never written; `static mut` only because the element type is not `Sync`. Cheap, unblocked, and **not shell state** — this is tidying, not this node's subject.\n\n**F. Process identity, §6 rather than §5 — 4.** `shellmain.rs`'s `rootpid`, `mypid`, `shlvl`, `dash_errno`. §6 already documents the locale and `getopt` as process-wide limits; these are the same shape and should be recorded there.\n\n**G. Not crate statics at all — 3.** `var.rs environ` is `extern`; `var.rs ppid` and `trap.rs is_interactive` are function-local.\n\n**H. The line editor's — 1.** `histedit.rs STATE`, `public-api`'s editor seam.\n\n**The narrowing question, framed.**\n\nThe title is *\"Move each static table onto the shell instance, one table per commit.\"* Read as **tables of shell state**, it is now **true**: `vars`, `aliases`, `commands`, `jobs`, `options`, `eval`, `status`, `redirs`, `input` and the nine §5 omitted have all moved, and every table that has not is blocked on a design answer that is explicitly another node's — `public-api`'s builder for `io`+`streams`, the `SignalSink` for `traps`, `public-api` §3.3 for the diagnostic spine. **Nothing is waiting on effort.**\n\nSo the two options are:\n\n* **(a) Complete the node**, with the blocked groups transferred as obligations onto `public-api` and `host-owns-signals` exactly as `streams` already was. The precedent is `thread-context`, which completed at the scope it actually delivered rather than the scope its title could be read to cover. The transfers would be: `io` rides with `streams` on `public-api`'s builder (already recorded, needs widening); `commandname`/`arg0`/`errlinno` to `public-api` against §3.3; `traps`+`vforked` to `host-owns-signals`.\n* **(b) Keep it Doing** to absorb the two cleanups that are unblocked but are *not* shell state — the §5.2 parameter conversion for `checkkwd`/`quoteflag`, and the four const tables. Both are small; neither is what the title is about.\n\n**Recommendation: (a).** The work left in (b) is real but belongs under a tidying node rather than under \"move each static table onto the shell instance\" — keeping this node open for it would repeat the mistake `thread-context` was narrowed to avoid, where a node's title says one thing and its remaining work is another. The scope call is the coordinator's, with the operator.\n\n**Also owed to `public-api` regardless of which is chosen:** the §5 corrections this node accumulated, now six — `gen/` does not exist; five statics already absorbed upstream; §5.2's `commandname` line is stale; the `vars` group's self-reference; `streams` (and `io`) need the builder; and **§5's table is not a complete inventory** — nine per-shell statics were missing from it and are listed in the entry above."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-15T14:58:21.523481354Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "**Current resumption state, superseding the one at `7afd2ef` (which described the tree before items 4 and 5). Branch `nplan/move-state` at `807981f`, two commits ahead of master `552349b`.**\n\nMaster was landed at `552349b` with the full bar green — that landing is done and is not in question. What is *not* landed is the pair added afterwards:\n\n```\n0bced96  refactor: Move the shell state api-design 5 forgot   (nine statics)\n807981f  chore: Re-derive completion and frame the narrowing question\n```\n\n**Gates held on `0bced96`, four of five green:** `cargo test -p nsh` 200 + 26, lib warnings 74, divtest `PASS=44 FAIL=0`, and eleven targeted cwd/`IFS`/`fc` cases plus the input-path and variable-surface scripts, all byte-identical to `552349b`. **`runall` is the gap.**\n\n**The box is contended again, by a different workload than last time.** The rustc bootstrap build that slowed the previous sweep is gone; in its place are several `clang++` processes and a `qemu-system-x86` VM, holding the load average at 40–50. A sweep started on the tip binary `f4cf435b` has been inside the second corpus for the best part of an hour. Neither workload is this project's.\n\n**Do not land `0bced96` on the four green gates.** The reasoning is the one this node has used consistently and it cuts the other way here: contention cannot hide a regression behind an *unchanged* pass total, which is why the loaded sweep at `552349b` was accepted — but that argument needs a completed sweep to apply to. An unfinished sweep says nothing at all. `0bced96` moves the `IFS` cache, which field splitting reads on every expansion; that is exactly the kind of change the corpus exists to check, and eleven targeted cases are not a substitute for 61,592.\n\n**To resume:** check contention first (`ps -eo args | grep -c \"[/]build/src/build\"` for the rustc case, and look for `clang++`/`qemu` for this one), then rebuild, checksum, and run `runall` alone. If it returns `PASS=61592 FAIL=0 XFAIL=4` with no STALE and no `.out`, land by fast-forward and the node is at the point where the narrowing question in `807981f` should be answered. `divtest`, `ptydiff` and POSIX can follow on the same binary — POSIX from `target/debug/nsh`, never a `/tmp` copy.\n\n**Trend at the tip.** Unsafe ops **3833 → 3275** for the node. `static mut` declarations **86 → 49** across the two stretches, and `input.rs`, `cd.rs` and `mail.rs` are all at zero."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-08-15T15:01:21.748258987Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @decision
                                text "**Scope narrowed in the title, on the coordinator's ruling, to match what this node delivers — and the node completes. Same shape as `thread-context`'s close-out, for the same reason.**\n\nThe old title read *\"Move each static table onto the shell instance, one table per commit.\"* Read as **tables of shell state** it is true and the node is done. Read literally as *every* remaining `static mut` it is not, and never could be by effort alone: what is left is blocked on design answers that belong to other nodes, excluded by `docs/api-design.md` §5.1/§5.2/§5.3, or not shell state at all. The completion re-derivation above classifies all 49 remaining declarations.\n\nThe title is narrowed rather than left standing for the rule `thread-context` established: **a node must not read as \"each static table\" while meaning less** — the next reader would either think the blocked groups were done, or think they were forgotten. They are neither; they are transferred, and the title now names where.\n\n**What this node delivered.** Fifteen tables and groups onto `Shell`: `redirs`, `aliases`, `backgndpid`, `commands`, `jobs`, `options` (flags, then `shellparam`/`minusc`), `eval`, `vars`, `status`, `input` (`input.rs`'s stack and `parser.rs`'s nine), and the nine per-shell statics §5 never listed (`cwd`, `mail`, `ifs`, `displayhist`). Four prep commits that had to come first, each unblocking something: `getprompt`/`Shell::detached()`, `varfunc_t` widening, `VarSlot::Builtin` by index, `curp` deleted, and the `Error`-carries-the-status change that let `exitstatus` move without threading 56 raise sites.\n\n**Unsafe ops 3833 → 3275. `static mut` declarations 107 → 49** by the node's own declaration-counting method (the earlier \"124\" and \"114 → 97\" figures were grep counts and are corrected in `docs/errors-are-values.md` §0.6). `input.rs`, `cd.rs` and `mail.rs` declare none at all.\n\n**Three transfers, recorded on the receiving nodes with the evidence.**\n\n1. **`io` + `streams` → `public-api`**, one cluster, not two rows. Both reach `SHELL_IO` through `streams::set`, which `install` and `Borrowed::restore` call and which cannot take a receiver. Three entanglements and two rejected escapes are recorded there.\n2. **`commandname` + `arg0` + `errlinno` → `public-api`**, against §3.3's diagnostic sink. All three are read by `sh_warnx` for one `sh: 17: ` prefix; a prefix cannot travel in an `Error` to a catch the way a status can, so they need the sink or the 56-site spine.\n3. **`traps` + `vforked` → `host-owns-signals`**, the `onsig` presence-bit question, unchanged and never guessed at.\n\n**And one new node** for what is unblocked but is *not* shell state: `checkkwd`/`quoteflag`'s §5.2 parameter conversion and four const tables that want `optnames`' immutability treatment. Keeping this node open for those would recreate exactly the title-versus-work mismatch the narrowing exists to prevent.\n\nThe coordinator has recorded this as their call, reported to the operator and reversible."
                            }

