                            {
                                at 2026-08-15T15:14:31.102810305Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "**Final gates, on `f4cf435b` (`0bced96`, the nine statics §5 omits). Green; the node's last commits are landed and `move-state` is closed.**\n\n```\nrunall      PASS=61592 FAIL=0 FLAKY=40 XFAIL=4, no STALE, zero .out\ndivtest     PASS=44 FAIL=0\nPOSIX       cases PASS=660 FAIL=51 -- the 51-name core EXACTLY,\n            zero missing, zero extra\ncargo test  200 + 26\nwarnings    74\n```\n\n**The sweep ran under heavier contention than any before it** — `clang++` and a `qemu-system-x86` VM, not this project's, taking the load average to 100 at its peak — and it is accepted on the coordinator's ruling and this node's own reasoning. `PASS=61592` is the figure every green sweep here has returned, with `FAIL=0`, `XFAIL=4` and no STALE. Contention manufactures false *failures*, never false passes, and a case that timed out would be classified rather than skipped; a regression cannot hide inside an unchanged pass total. What load costs is wall clock and `FLAKY`, and the eighteen files left in `tests/.build/fail/` are all `.flaky` or `.xfail`, with **no `.out` at all**.\n\n**`ptydiff` was not re-run for this commit, deliberately, and the reason is the rule this node recorded rather than an omission.** That rule cuts both ways: *when a change touches a path the corpus structurally cannot execute, the corpus being green is not evidence about it* — and equally, when a change does **not** touch such a path, the pty suite adds nothing the other gates have not already covered. `0bced96` moves `cd.rs`'s cwd pair, `mail.rs`'s mailbox times, `expand.rs`'s `IFS` cache and `histedit.rs`'s `displayhist`. **None is on the line-editor read path** — that was `0f1da0e`'s `preadfd`, and `ptydiff` was run to completion on it at `552349b` with `PASS=43 FAIL=0 FLAKY=0`, including both `fc -l` editing cases. `displayhist` is `fc -l`'s own flag and is covered by the POSIX `fc` cases, which pass here. The `IFS` cache is exercised by every field split in the 61,592-case corpus.\n\n**The node's full arc.**\n\n```\nunsafe ops              3833 -> 3275   (-558)\nstatic mut declarations  107 ->   49   (-58, declaration-counted)\nfiles at zero            —   -> input.rs, cd.rs, mail.rs\n```\n\nFifteen tables and groups moved onto `Shell`; five prep commits that had to come first; six corrections to `docs/api-design.md` §5 recorded for `public-api`, the last of which is that §5's table was never a complete inventory. Three obligations transferred with their evidence, and one new node for the remainder that is not shell state."
