                        text "Completion result, re-derived from the final tree. All mutable shell state is instance-owned; `crates/nsh`, `nsh-cli`, and the embed example contain zero `static mut`, zero unsafe declarations/blocks/attributes, and zero `libc::` references. `nsh` and `nsh-cli` both deny `unsafe_code`. The call-scoped parser state became typed arguments/returns; immutable C-shaped tables became safe Rust tables; the expansion/eval/parser/builtin cascades are ordinary safe functions. The arithmetic `arith_yylex.rs` module and `yylex` function are deleted: `arith_yacc.rs` now owns a typed lexer and recursive-descent parser with token values and lookahead held per evaluation. All per-shell variables, jobs, options, redirections, streams, input, output, history and scratch buffers live on `Shell` or call frames.\n\nFinal gates on the exact source: `cargo test --workspace` 253 passed (plus one ignored doctest); full differential with the inherited FD hard limit PASS=61768 FAIL=0 FLAKY=25 XFAIL=4, no STALE/invalid corpus; divergence-register self-test 44/0; sandboxed PTY 60/0/0; POSIX target 660/51 vs C dash 655/56, with no target-only locale regression; annotations valid, dash 422/422 covered, 34 tested, 0 stale. `git diff --check` clean."
