                        kind @note
                        text "Completion result. Added `crates/nsh-platform`, whose 102 public functions are safe wrappers; it is the workspace's sole direct `libc` dependency and the only crate containing unsafe syntax. `nsh`, `nsh-cli`, and the embed example have zero unsafe/libc/static-mut and both binaries/libraries deny unsafe code. The old 255 direct `libc` call sites and 13 hand-declared symbols in `nsh` are gone. The platform floor is down to 33 direct libc calls in 22 contained unsafe blocks plus two ABI declaration blocks. What remains is behavior-bearing ABI/process work: pre-runtime inherited-process-state capture, locale ctype/collation/multibyte conversion, named-account lookup for `~user`, exact execve pointer arrays, arbitrary numeric/real-time signals and sigaction/masks/sigsuspend, times(2), raw inherited-fd dup/close, fork, PID-namespace process-group zero handling, and localized strsignal text. Replacing those would either lose dash/POSIX behavior or merely move the same unsafe into another dependency.\n\nAvoidable libc was replaced with std/rustix throughout: `std::process::id`, `ExitStatusExt`, owned environment/path types, safe directory/stat/access/resource/wait/terminal/pipe calls, `OpenOptions::create_new` 0600 temp files, safe OS error rendering, and rustix's safe `exit_group`. Bare `~` continues to use the individual Shell's `$HOME`; `std::env::home_dir` cannot answer `~other-user`, so only that named-account case reaches the passwd wrapper. The CLI already terminates through `std::process::exit`. A forked child cannot: a parallel test caught it deadlocking, and gdb showed `std::process::exit -> std::rt::cleanup -> stack_overflow::drop_handler -> Mutex::lock` on a lock whose owner existed only before fork. `exit_immediately` therefore uses safe `rustix::runtime::exit_group`, with no libc or unsafe at the call site. `vfork` was removed in favor of `fork` after the shared-address-space port corrupted Rust heap/stack state.\n\nValidation on the final source: workspace 253/0; exhaustive differential 61768/0 with 25 classified scheduling flakes and 4 sanctioned divergences; divergence register 44/0; PTY 60/0/0; POSIX 660/51 vs C dash 655/56; annotations clean, dash coverage 422/422 and 0 stale. The POSIX pass caught and fixed one typed-callback regression where explicit `LC_ALL=` had been conflated with unset; a unit test now pins the distinction."
                    }

