                        kind @note
                        text "Implemented the model correction. Each Shell now owns a ten-slot FdTable; open slots share close-on-exec OwnedFd backing handles above the language range. Builtin output, input, redirection save/restore, pipelines, command substitution, background stdin, terminal probes and line editing resolve logical slots without mutating the host descriptor table. Streams::install, RawFd, DescriptorSlot, replace/move/clear exact-slot APIs, numeric close, and the redundant ParseFile fd shadow are gone. FdTable::materialize constructs a validated ProcessFdChanges transaction immediately before exec; its private platform implementation contains the only remaining libc::dup2 and libc::close calls. NoHost refuses root image replacement before materialization; forked children and ProcessHost termini may exec. Red tests now prove supplied stdout reaches direct external commands and pipelines and survives command-scoped redirection. Validation on the final tree: cargo check --workspace --all-targets; cargo test --workspace (253 passed, 1 ignored doctest); embed example; differential PASS=39349 FAIL=0 FLAKY=25 XFAIL=4; divergence register PASS=44 FAIL=0; PTY PASS=60 FAIL=0 FLAKY=0; POSIX target PASS=660 FAIL=51 versus C dash PASS=655 FAIL=56. Final searches: zero RawFd/DescriptorSlot/ambient exact-slot APIs in crates, zero unsafe code in nsh, and exactly one dup2 plus one close in ProcessFdChanges. Documented surviving semantic gap: builtin opens of /dev/fd/N-style paths observe the kernel table until an exec terminus materializes the logical map."
